import{_ as t,o as i,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const c=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 409 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Ji Ning vs. Tang Luo: Predatory vs. Gift-Style Comparison","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 409 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Ji Ning vs. Tang Luo: Predatory vs. Gift-Style Comparison","no":409,"module":2,"tags":["Manghuang Ji","Ji Ning","Tang Luo","Predatory","Gift-Style","Comparison"],"related":["251-Tang-Luo System Decomposition Overview","261-Tang-Luo Enlightened-Predator Verdict","04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0409_模块2-莽荒纪-纪宁vs唐罗-掠夺式与恩赐式对比.md","filePath":"en/0409_模块2-莽荒纪-纪宁vs唐罗-掠夺式与恩赐式对比.md"}'),a={name:"en/0409_模块2-莽荒纪-纪宁vs唐罗-掠夺式与恩赐式对比.md"};function s(r,e,l,d,g,h){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-409-manghuang-system-decomposition-·-ji-ning-vs-tang-luo-predatory-vs-gift-style-comparison" tabindex="-1">Entry 409 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Ji Ning vs. Tang Luo: Predatory vs. Gift-Style Comparison <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-409-manghuang-system-decomposition-·-ji-ning-vs-tang-luo-predatory-vs-gift-style-comparison" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 409 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Ji Ning vs. Tang Luo: Predatory vs. Gift-Style Comparison&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Manghuang Ji Full Decomposition (Entry 14) | Benchmark base: Documents 251, 261, 04</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-one-directly-grabs-one-gives-out-pieces-—-actually-two-ways-of-sitting-at-the-same-table" tabindex="-1">Introduction: one directly grabs, one gives out pieces — actually two ways of sitting at the same table <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-one-directly-grabs-one-gives-out-pieces-—-actually-two-ways-of-sitting-at-the-same-table" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: one directly grabs, one gives out pieces — actually two ways of sitting at the same table&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The six top-level axioms open with the anti-predation axiom and take the law-first axiom as core. This entry compares two key benchmark protagonists: <em>I Can See Combat Power</em>&#39;s Tang Luo (gift-style / high dependency) and Manghuang&#39;s Ji Ning (predatory lone-path / high-leaning-medium dependency). Tang Luo is the typical &quot;enlightened predator&quot; — he breaks aristocratic monopoly, universalizes martial path, but high-tier Great Dao is private, grace tied to one person; Ji Ning cannot even be bothered to &quot;universal benefit,&quot; directly takes resources by strength. This entry distinguishes the two&#39;s similarities and differences. Protagonist uniqueness dependency: Ji Ning = high-leaning-medium, Tang Luo = high. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s judging base has been upgraded to the six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The two&#39;s waste directions differ: Tang Luo&#39;s energy is wasted on &quot;gift-style administration&quot; — he spends large effort rebuilding Peerless Academy, personally universalizing martial path; energy direction is civilization infrastructure but limited in scale; Ji Ning&#39;s energy is wasted on &quot;personal leveling&quot; — all resources piled on himself, infrastructure almost zero. <strong>Tang Luo at least built a school; Ji Ning did not even build one.</strong></p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The two&#39;s regression mechanisms compared:</p><ol><li><strong>Tang Luo = gift-style regression</strong>: universal benefit is given by the strong; the patron absent and it breaks</li><li><strong>Ji Ning = predatory regression</strong>: resources are grabbed; the strong stops grabbing and fighting reignites</li><li><strong>Common lesion</strong>: both bet order on one person; neither built &quot;tea not cooling when person leaves&quot; institutions</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The two&#39;s predation key differences:</p><ul><li><strong>Tang Luo = implicit predation</strong>: he universal-benefits humankind&#39;s lower-middle tier, but privately hoards high-tier Great Dao — the gentlest predation makes people accustomed to being alms-given</li><li><strong>Ji Ning = explicit predation</strong>: he directly devours resources, seizes secret realms, never pretends universal benefit — the most honest predation never pretends it is for your own good</li><li><strong>Who is worse?</strong>: on Myriad Ranks&#39; coverage, Tang Luo only benefits humankind, Ji Ning does not even benefit humankind; on institutional consciousness, Tang Luo at least has the &quot;academy&quot; prototype, Ji Ning has none. <strong>Both are people atop the predatory pyramid, only one wears a hat and one does not.</strong></li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Tang Luo (Gift-Style / High)</th><th>Ji Ning (Predatory / High-Leaning-Medium)</th><th>Anchor Symbiosis</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Resource allocation</td><td>Strong one alms-gives</td><td>Strong one grabs</td><td>Jointly contracted, more work more pay</td></tr><tr><td>Knowledge open</td><td>Lower-middle open, high-tier private</td><td>All private</td><td>All-tier public, no private Dao</td></tr><tr><td>Institutional prototype</td><td>Peerless Academy</td><td>None</td><td>Anchor Council + Alaya Network</td></tr><tr><td>Myriad Ranks coverage</td><td>Humankind only</td><td>Humankind top only</td><td>Myriad Ranks 99% full coverage</td></tr><tr><td>Protagonist absent</td><td>Universal-benefit breaks</td><td>Fighting reignites</td><td>Network-style civilization runs as usual</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate &quot;Tang Luo gift,&quot; &quot;Ji Ning predation,&quot; &quot;Anchor Symbiosis&quot; three civilizations&#39; initial parameters</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: uniformly inject &quot;protagonist exits&quot; shock; observe three civilizations&#39; evolution</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: institutional-takeover rate, Myriad-Ranks self-rescue rate, knowledge-inheritance rate</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: quantified conclusion — Tang Luo model relies on academy prototype to take over part, Ji Ning model directly collapses, Anchor-Symbiosis model steadiest; but the former two both far below the symbiotic model</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: Tang Luo medium-high vs. Ji Ning medium-low</strong>. Tang Luo realms capped, rules internally self-consistent; Ji Ning dragged by inflation and linkage</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: Tang Luo medium vs. Ji Ning high</strong></li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: Tang Luo high vs. Ji Ning high-leaning-medium</strong> — Tang Luo more dependent on personal good will, Ji Ning more dependent on personal combat strength</li></ul><p>Tang Luo and Ji Ning also have a key difference: Tang Luo at least admits he is giving; Ji Ning does not even have the concept of giving. Tang Luo&#39;s problem is grace; Ji Ning&#39;s problem is even grace is saved — he defaults resources should be his. This means reforming Manghuang is harder than reforming Tang Luo: Tang Luo only needs to learn to let go; Ji Ning needs to learn that this thing was not his to begin with. From predation to grace is still progress; from grace to co-build is the endpoint. Both are still halfway, just stopped at different positions.</p><p>Putting Tang Luo and Ji Ning on one table also reveals the &quot;kindness&quot; gradient. Tang Luo&#39;s kindness has a boundary, he only benefits humankind; Ji Ning&#39;s kindness cannot even be bothered to think about a boundary. But Heng Yuan Zhou does not reward the kindness gradient; it rewards structural root reform. No matter how far kindness goes, as long as the bottom jurisprudence is still zero-sum, it is still within the predation lineage.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: Tang Luo wasted on gift administration, Ji Ning wasted on personal leveling</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: implicit predation and explicit predation both stand atop the pyramid</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: this entry is the comparison — Tang Luo at least universal-benefits humankind, Ji Ning does not even universal-benefit</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: both only cover humankind; Myriad Ranks share none</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: both grace and predation have not touched open-cosmos institutional design</li></ul><p>Tang Luo and Ji Ning&#39;s comparison can also extend to &quot;institutional imagination.&quot; Tang Luo at least thought of building an academy, though the academy is also gift-style; Ji Ning did not even have the thought of &quot;set up some institution&quot;; in his world there are only enemies and himself. This shows predatory protagonists not only plunder resources, but also plunder imagination — he cannot imagine an order not relying on personal strong-arm rule. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s four bodies — Anchor Council, Symbiotic Executive Committee, Symbiotic Court, Inspection Committee — are precisely the reverse proof of this imagination.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Tang Luo wears a hat, Ji Ning does not, but they sit at the same predatory table. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s judgment is not &quot;who is worse,&quot; but &quot;should this table be flipped&quot; — grace and predation both do not solve the problem; the true alternative is changing the table to Myriad Ranks&#39; own dining table.</p><p>In the final analysis, Manghuang Ji · Ji Ning vs. Tang Luo · predatory vs. gift-style comparison described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./408_模块2-莽荒纪-纪宁vs古尘沙-两种孤道体系的差异.html">Entry 408 · Ji Ning vs. Gu Chensha</a> · <a href="./410_模块2-莽荒纪-纪宁vs叶凡-莽荒与遮天的孤道传承.html">Entry 410 · Ji Ning vs. Ye Fan</a> · <a href="./../../文库试点/251_模块2-唐罗体系拆解-总论三重上限与主角唯一性评判.html">251-Tang-Luo System Decomposition Overview</a></li></ul>',29)])])}const m=t(a,[["render",s]]);export{c as __pageData,m as default};
